<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n112213" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φρᾰδ-ή</span></b> , ἡ, poet.
		Noun, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>understanding,
				knowledge,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῶν δὲ μελλόντων τετύφλωνται φραδαί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pi.
					<u>O.</u>
					12.9
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Alc.
				<u>Supp.</u>
				2.2
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>hint, warning,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θεόθεν . . φραδαῖσιν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Ch.</u>
					941
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.), cf. <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Ph.</u>
				667
			</span></i> (lyr.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀθανάτων φραδῇ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Theoc.
					25.52
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				5(2).261.15
			</span></i> (Mantinea, <span class="entity">vi B. C.</span>); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἕπου μηνυτῆρος ἀφθέγκτου φραδαῖς,</span> i. e. by the
			scent, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Eu.</u>
				245
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
